### prop:consequence -- the five non-certificate hypotheses
sage version      : SageMath version 10.7, Release Date: 2025-08-09
curve             : Elliptic Curve defined by y^2 = x^3 - 56*x over Rational Field
minimal model     : [0, 0, 0, -56, 0]
conductor N       : 12544 = 2^8 * 7^2
discriminant      : 11239424 = 2^15 * 7^3
j-invariant       : 1728
CM                : by the order of discriminant -4 in K = Q(i)
rank              : 2
torsion order     : 2
Tamagawa product  : 4
K = Q(i), d_K     : -4
6N*prod c_v*#tors*|d_K| = 6*12544*4*2*4 = 2408448 = 2^14 * 3 * 7^2
   => the eq:Sexc divisibility condition is supported on [2, 3, 7]
isogeny class     : 2 curves, isogeny matrix degrees [1, 2]
   => every isogeny in the class has 2-power degree, so E admits no rational
      p-isogeny for odd p, so rhobar_{E,p} is irreducible for every odd p.

